-- Named example values shared by the tests and the census. Every record is written out
-- field by field with WITH, never positionally: these records have many BOOLEAN fields,
-- and positional OF construction is silently order-dependent.
--
-- Contents built from fixture files take their manifest from fixture-manifests.l4,
-- which is GENERATED from the files by c2patool. Everything else here is a supposition
-- about the scenario, written by hand, and says so.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `labelling-domain`
IMPORT `fixture-manifests`
IMPORT `eu-ai-act-art50`
IMPORT `wa-e2shb-1170`
IMPORT `ca-bpc-22757`

§ `Dates`

`1 August 2026`     MEANS YMD 2026  8  1
`2 August 2026`     MEANS YMD 2026  8  2
`15 September 2026` MEANS YMD 2026  9 15
`29 September 2026` MEANS YMD 2026  9 29
`30 September 2026` MEANS YMD 2026  9 30
`1 October 2026`    MEANS YMD 2026 10  1
`1 December 2026`   MEANS YMD 2026 12  1
`2 December 2026`   MEANS YMD 2026 12  2
`31 December 2026`  MEANS YMD 2026 12 31
`1 January 2027`    MEANS YMD 2027  1  1
`31 January 2027`   MEANS YMD 2027  1 31
`1 February 2027`   MEANS YMD 2027  2  1
`31 December 2028`  MEANS YMD 2028 12 31
`1 January 2029`    MEANS YMD 2029  1  1

§ `Providers`

-- The base case: a public consumer generator, big enough for every regime, adhering to
-- the EU Code, placed on the EU market after 2 August 2026, named as the fixtures name
-- their generator.
GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A `the provider of the AI system`
`a large consumer provider named` n MEANS `the provider of the AI system` WITH
    `its name`                                                                  IS n
    `it is a state, local, or tribal government`                                IS FALSE
    `the monthly users of its system`                                           IS 5000000
    `its system is publicly accessible in Washington to consumers for personal use` IS TRUE
    `its system is publicly accessible within California`                       IS TRUE
    `the use is business-to-business`                                           IS FALSE
    `its system was placed on the EU market before 2 August 2026`               IS FALSE
    `it adheres to Section 1 of the EU Code of Practice`                        IS TRUE
    `its system is used solely for upscaling, noise reduction, or compression`  IS FALSE
    `its product exclusively provides video games or interactive experiences`   IS FALSE
    `its product exclusively provides non-user-generated videogames`            IS FALSE
    `its system is designed to primarily function as assistive technology`     IS FALSE
    `the use is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences` IS FALSE

`the generator` MEANS `a large consumer provider named` "babel-fixture-generator"
`the editor`    MEANS `a large consumer provider named` "babel-fixture-editor"

-- One fact changed at a time from the base case, so each test isolates one limb.
GIVEN users IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `the provider of the AI system`
`the generator, with monthly users numbering` users MEANS `the provider of the AI system` WITH
    `its name`                                                                  IS "babel-fixture-generator"
    `it is a state, local, or tribal government`                                IS FALSE
    `the monthly users of its system`                                           IS users
    `its system is publicly accessible in Washington to consumers for personal use` IS TRUE
    `its system is publicly accessible within California`                       IS TRUE
    `the use is business-to-business`                                           IS FALSE
    `its system was placed on the EU market before 2 August 2026`               IS FALSE
    `it adheres to Section 1 of the EU Code of Practice`                        IS TRUE
    `its system is used solely for upscaling, noise reduction, or compression`  IS FALSE
    `its product exclusively provides video games or interactive experiences`   IS FALSE
    `its product exclusively provides non-user-generated videogames`            IS FALSE
    `its system is designed to primarily function as assistive technology`     IS FALSE
    `the use is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences` IS FALSE

-- A provider whose system was already on the EU market before 2 August 2026 (Art. 111(4)).
`a legacy generator` MEANS `the provider of the AI system` WITH
    `its name`                                                                  IS "babel-fixture-generator"
    `it is a state, local, or tribal government`                                IS FALSE
    `the monthly users of its system`                                           IS 5000000
    `its system is publicly accessible in Washington to consumers for personal use` IS TRUE
    `its system is publicly accessible within California`                       IS TRUE
    `the use is business-to-business`                                           IS FALSE
    `its system was placed on the EU market before 2 August 2026`               IS TRUE
    `it adheres to Section 1 of the EU Code of Practice`                        IS TRUE
    `its system is used solely for upscaling, noise reduction, or compression`  IS FALSE
    `its product exclusively provides video games or interactive experiences`   IS FALSE
    `its product exclusively provides non-user-generated videogames`            IS FALSE
    `its system is designed to primarily function as assistive technology`     IS FALSE
    `the use is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences` IS FALSE

-- Each of the remaining flags, set alone. Written out in full for the reason given above.
DECLARE `one changed fact` IS ONE OF
    `does not adhere to the Code`
    `is a government`
    `is used business-to-business`
    `is not accessible in Washington for personal use`
    `is not accessible in California`
    `is used solely for upscaling, noise reduction, or compression`
    `is a video game or interactive experience product`
    `is a non-user-generated videogame product`
    `is assistive technology`
    `is authorised for law enforcement`

GIVEN c IS A `one changed fact`
GIVETH A `the provider of the AI system`
`the generator, except that it` c MEANS `the provider of the AI system` WITH
    `its name`                                                                  IS "babel-fixture-generator"
    `it is a state, local, or tribal government`                                IS c EQUALS `is a government`
    `the monthly users of its system`                                           IS 5000000
    `its system is publicly accessible in Washington to consumers for personal use` IS NOT c EQUALS `is not accessible in Washington for personal use`
    `its system is publicly accessible within California`                       IS NOT c EQUALS `is not accessible in California`
    `the use is business-to-business`                                           IS c EQUALS `is used business-to-business`
    `its system was placed on the EU market before 2 August 2026`               IS FALSE
    `it adheres to Section 1 of the EU Code of Practice`                        IS NOT c EQUALS `does not adhere to the Code`
    `its system is used solely for upscaling, noise reduction, or compression`  IS c EQUALS `is used solely for upscaling, noise reduction, or compression`
    `its product exclusively provides video games or interactive experiences`   IS c EQUALS `is a video game or interactive experience product`
    `its product exclusively provides non-user-generated videogames`            IS c EQUALS `is a non-user-generated videogame product`
    `its system is designed to primarily function as assistive technology`     IS c EQUALS `is assistive technology`
    `the use is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences` IS c EQUALS `is authorised for law enforcement`

§ `Contents`

-- From fixture files: what the file is is fixed by the file; what an AI system did to
-- it is the scenario's supposition, consistent with what its manifest records.
GIVEN kinds IS A LIST OF `kind of content`
      how   IS A `how the content came to exist`
      alts  IS A LIST OF `kind of alteration`
      m     IS A MAYBE `C2PA manifest`
      w     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `piece of content`
`content of kinds` kinds `that came to exist by` how `altered by` alts `carrying` m `watermarked` w MEANS `piece of content` WITH
    `the kinds it contains`                   IS kinds
    `how it came to exist`                    IS how
    `the alterations an AI system made to it` IS alts
    `the C2PA manifest it carries`            IS m
    `it carries an imperceptible watermark`   IS w
    `it is very short text`                   IS FALSE
    `it stays inside a closed physical product` IS FALSE

`the camera capture` MEANS
    `content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `captured by a capture device` `altered by` EMPTY `carrying` `the manifest of c2pa-rs-camera-capture` `watermarked` FALSE
-- CA.jpg records c2pa.color_adjustments; the scenario supposes an AI system made them.
`the colour-adjusted photo` MEANS
    `content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `captured by a capture device` `altered by` (LIST `a change to brightness, contrast, or color`) `carrying` `the manifest of c2pa-rs-colour-adjusted` `watermarked` FALSE
`the AI-generated image` MEANS
    `content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `generated by an AI system` `altered by` EMPTY `carrying` `the manifest of ai-generated` `watermarked` FALSE
-- The manifest DECLARES a watermark; the scenario supposes the watermark is really there.
`the AI-generated image with a watermark` MEANS
    `content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `generated by an AI system` `altered by` EMPTY `carrying` `the manifest of ai-generated-watermark-declared` `watermarked` TRUE
`the AI-generated image, stripped` MEANS
    `content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `generated by an AI system` `altered by` EMPTY `carrying` `the manifest of ai-generated-stripped` `watermarked` FALSE
`the photo with an object removed` MEANS
    `content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `captured by a capture device` `altered by` (LIST `removal, replacement or insertion of an object or person`) `carrying` `the manifest of ai-object-removed` `watermarked` FALSE
`the filtered photo` MEANS
    `content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `captured by a capture device` `altered by` (LIST `applying a filter`) `carrying` `the manifest of ai-filtered` `watermarked` FALSE
`the photo with red-eye removed` MEANS
    `content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `captured by a capture device` `altered by` (LIST `removal of red-eye or dust spots`) `carrying` `the manifest of ai-red-eye-removed` `watermarked` FALSE

-- Synthetic contents with no fixture file.
GIVEN alts IS A LIST OF `kind of alteration`
GIVETH A `piece of content`
`a photo an AI system altered by` alts MEANS
    `content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `captured by a capture device` `altered by` alts `carrying` NOTHING `watermarked` FALSE

`an AI-written article` MEANS `piece of content` WITH
    `the kinds it contains`                   IS LIST `free-form text`
    `how it came to exist`                    IS `generated by an AI system`
    `the alterations an AI system made to it` IS EMPTY
    `the C2PA manifest it carries`            IS NOTHING
    `it carries an imperceptible watermark`   IS TRUE
    `it is very short text`                   IS FALSE
    `it stays inside a closed physical product` IS FALSE

`an AI-written caption of eight words` MEANS `piece of content` WITH
    `the kinds it contains`                   IS LIST `free-form text`
    `how it came to exist`                    IS `generated by an AI system`
    `the alterations an AI system made to it` IS EMPTY
    `the C2PA manifest it carries`            IS NOTHING
    `it carries an imperceptible watermark`   IS FALSE
    `it is very short text`                   IS TRUE
    `it stays inside a closed physical product` IS FALSE

`an AI image inside a closed training simulator` MEANS `piece of content` WITH
    `the kinds it contains`                   IS LIST `image`
    `how it came to exist`                    IS `generated by an AI system`
    `the alterations an AI system made to it` IS EMPTY
    `the C2PA manifest it carries`            IS NOTHING
    `it carries an imperceptible watermark`   IS TRUE
    `it is very short text`                   IS FALSE
    `it stays inside a closed physical product` IS TRUE

`a photo nobody altered` MEANS
    `content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `captured by a capture device` `altered by` EMPTY `carrying` NOTHING `watermarked` FALSE

§ `Publications (EU Art. 50(4))`

GIVEN personal IS A BOOLEAN, resembles IS A BOOLEAN, publicInterest IS A BOOLEAN, reviewed IS A BOOLEAN, responsible IS A BOOLEAN, police IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `the publication`
`a publication where personal use is` personal `it resembles real things` resembles `public-interest text` publicInterest `human-reviewed` reviewed `someone responsible` responsible `law enforcement` police MEANS `the publication` WITH
    `the deployer uses the AI system in the course of a personal non-professional activity` IS personal
    `the content resembles existing persons, objects, places, entities or events`            IS resembles
    `the text is published with the purpose of informing the public on matters of public interest` IS publicInterest
    `the text has undergone a process of human review or editorial control`                  IS reviewed
    `a natural or legal person holds editorial responsibility for the publication`           IS responsible
    `the use is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences` IS police

`a business publishing a lifelike image` MEANS
    `a publication where personal use is` FALSE `it resembles real things` TRUE `public-interest text` FALSE `human-reviewed` FALSE `someone responsible` FALSE `law enforcement` FALSE
`a private person posting a lifelike image` MEANS
    `a publication where personal use is` TRUE `it resembles real things` TRUE `public-interest text` FALSE `human-reviewed` FALSE `someone responsible` FALSE `law enforcement` FALSE
`a business publishing an image of nothing real` MEANS
    `a publication where personal use is` FALSE `it resembles real things` FALSE `public-interest text` FALSE `human-reviewed` FALSE `someone responsible` FALSE `law enforcement` FALSE
`a news site publishing unreviewed AI text` MEANS
    `a publication where personal use is` FALSE `it resembles real things` FALSE `public-interest text` TRUE `human-reviewed` FALSE `someone responsible` FALSE `law enforcement` FALSE
`a newspaper publishing edited AI text` MEANS
    `a publication where personal use is` FALSE `it resembles real things` FALSE `public-interest text` TRUE `human-reviewed` TRUE `someone responsible` TRUE `law enforcement` FALSE
`a news site publishing reviewed AI text nobody is responsible for` MEANS
    `a publication where personal use is` FALSE `it resembles real things` FALSE `public-interest text` TRUE `human-reviewed` TRUE `someone responsible` FALSE `law enforcement` FALSE
`a police unit publishing a lifelike image` MEANS
    `a publication where personal use is` FALSE `it resembles real things` TRUE `public-interest text` FALSE `human-reviewed` FALSE `someone responsible` FALSE `law enforcement` TRUE

§ `Platforms (CA 22757.3.1)`

GIVEN kind IS A BOOLEAN, others IS A BOOLEAN, users IS A NUMBER, broadband IS A BOOLEAN, telecom IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `the distributing platform`
`a platform where it is a listed kind` kind `distributing to others` others `with users` users `a broadband service` broadband `a telecom service` telecom MEANS `the distributing platform` WITH
    `it is a public-facing social media platform, file-sharing platform, mass messaging platform, or stand-alone search engine` IS kind
    `it distributes content to users who did not create or collaborate in creating the content` IS others
    `its unique monthly users during the preceding 12 months` IS users
    `it is a broadband internet access service`               IS broadband
    `it is a telecommunications service`                      IS telecom

`a large social network` MEANS
    `a platform where it is a listed kind` TRUE `distributing to others` TRUE `with users` 50000000 `a broadband service` FALSE `a telecom service` FALSE

§ `Judgements`

GIVEN standard IS A BOOLEAN, notSubstantial IS A BOOLEAN, falselyAuthentic IS A BOOLEAN, artistic IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `EU Article 50 judgements`
`EU judgements: standard editing` standard `, not substantial` notSubstantial `, falsely authentic` falselyAuthentic `, artistic` artistic MEANS `EU Article 50 judgements` WITH
    `the AI system performs an assistive function for standard editing`                        IS standard
    `the AI system does not substantially alter the input data provided by the deployer or the semantics thereof` IS notSubstantial
    `the content would falsely appear to a person to be authentic or truthful`                 IS falselyAuthentic
    `the content forms part of an evidently artistic, creative, satirical, fictional or analogous work or programme` IS artistic

-- Generation from a prompt, or a substantive edit: neither exception, a lifelike result.
`EU: a substantive, lifelike output` MEANS `EU judgements: standard editing` FALSE `, not substantial` FALSE `, falsely authentic` TRUE `, artistic` FALSE
-- The Guidelines' para 92 examples of standard editing.
`EU: standard editing` MEANS `EU judgements: standard editing` TRUE `, not substantial` TRUE `, falsely authentic` FALSE `, artistic` FALSE

GIVEN significant IS A BOOLEAN, reasonable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Washington section 2 judgements`
`Washington judgements: significant change` significant `, reasonable` reasonable MEANS `Washington section 2 judgements` WITH
    `the alteration is a significant change that substantially alters the data in content` IS significant
    `including provenance data is commercially and technically reasonable`                 IS reasonable

`WA: significant and reasonable` MEANS `Washington judgements: significant change` TRUE `, reasonable` TRUE
`WA: not significant`            MEANS `Washington judgements: significant change` FALSE `, reasonable` TRUE

GIVEN feasible IS A BOOLEAN, permanent IS A BOOLEAN, compatible IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `California 22757.3 inputs`
`California inputs: feasible` feasible `, permanent` permanent `, compatible` compatible MEANS `California 22757.3 inputs` WITH
    `including a latent disclosure is technically feasible`                     IS feasible
    `the disclosure is permanent or extraordinarily difficult to remove or tamper with` IS permanent
    `the disclosure is compatible with the covered provider's disclosure verification tool` IS compatible

`CA: feasible, permanent, compatible` MEANS `California inputs: feasible` TRUE `, permanent` TRUE `, compatible` TRUE
`CA: feasible, removable, compatible` MEANS `California inputs: feasible` TRUE `, permanent` FALSE `, compatible` TRUE
